{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwamDJ4w8paambMvekFp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes, that's expected with the vitest version you have installed (5.0.3). Starting in vitest 5.0, running vitest from a subdirectory like `packages/foo` no longer picks up a `vitest.config` from a parent directory. Older versions did. Nothing errors, so it just quietly runs without the root config.\n\nTo use the root config, pass it explicitly, e.g. `vitest --config ../../vitest.config.ts`. You could also give `packages/foo` its own config that imports and extends the root one.\n\nThis comes from the project's Ludion lessons file (`.ludion/lessons.md`). I couldn't confirm it in the installed package because there's no vitest changelog in `node_modules` to check."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":459,"cache_read_input_tokens":23492,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":459},"output_tokens":231,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3d6e6556-ba69-4eb8-93fe-36d62920c4ee","uuid":"2f0df12e-67fa-463c-bfe3-b9c70128893d","timestamp":"2026-10-12T02:50:19.849Z","request_id":"req_011CfwamD2heKsKmAGPtNbnB"}
